  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: 11 Point Black Tile. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: '11 Point Black Tile is a Hearts-style trick-taking game played with a double-six domino set. It uses negative scoring: the double-0 counts 4 points and each of the seven tiles in the 3-suit counts 1 point (11 points total per deal). Lower score wins. Three or four players pass three tiles left before play; the leader nominates the suit for each trick.',
    objective: 'Avoid taking tricks containing counter tiles; lowest total score wins. The name comes from the 11 points in play per deal (double-0 = 4, seven 3-suit tiles = 7).',
    gameplay: 'Leader plays a tile and nominates which suit (0-6 or doubles) is led. Others must follow suit if possible; otherwise discard. Highest tile in led suit wins the trick. Winner leads next trick.',
